  "result": "Completion now handles arguments containing `#`. The parser and shell-completion tests pass (68 passed).\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default. Everything after a `#` was dropped, so `cli a#b` completed as `cli a`.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character.\n\n**Tests:** I added three cases to `tests/test_parser.py`: `a#b`, a leading `#a`, and `#` inside an unclosed quote.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry. The top section there is already the released 8.5.0, and I don't know which version this should go under.",
